{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Before the eyes of all Israel.</b> I have heard them say a reason for why the Torah begins with בֵּי״ת and concludes with לָמֶ״ד — for all the letters of the great Name, יוּ״ד וָ״ו הֵ״א, if you attach any one of them to a בֵּי״ת or to a לָמֶ״ד, there will emerge from it a single complete word, and they are: בִּי, בּוֹ, בָּהּ, לִי, לוֹ, לָהּ. Something you will not find in any other alphabet-letter — that a complete word would result from all three [letters of the Name] if they were attached to a given letter; for example, making from אָלֶ״ף: אִי or אָהּ — but אָהּ is not a word; and likewise making from מֶ״ם: מִי, מוּ — but מוּ is not a word. And the explanation of this is that therein is hinted that the world and its fullness — all depend on Him, blessed be He, and to Him belongs everything. And the form of the בֵּי״ת, by which the Holy One, blessed be He, speaks on His own behalf and says 'בִּי' — that is to say, everything depends on Me; and His creatures say 'בּוֹ' — that everything depends on Him, blessed be He. And the expressions 'בּוֹ' 'בָּהּ' are masculine and feminine, which the masters of truth among the kabbalists mentioned. And likewise the Holy One, blessed be He, says: לִי — the world and its fullness are Mine; and His creatures say, for to Him, blessed be He, belong the world and its fullness. And likewise 'לָהּ' by way of the same explanation, and it is all one matter, for since everything depends on Him, blessed be He, therefore everything is His, blessed be He. And this is a hint to His oneness, blessed be He, which is the foundation of the Torah. And this matter — He is the opener and the closer; therefore the Torah opened with בֵּי״ת and concludes with לָמֶ״ד, to indicate that HaShem, blessed be He, is the opener and the closer, and all depends on Him, in His name, blessed be He, as stated above. <br> <b>Completed is the book of Devarim, with the help of the Former of all creatures.</b>"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:16:52.493965140Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}